Hi,
As long as SRM recognizes the pci video card and XFree86 version 
you are using supports the card, you can run Xsessions.
For the PWS- matrox(MII,G200,G450), glint Permedia2,3[3D-labs, 4D20
etc], ATI cards up to the radeon 7500 are supported, not supported by
SRM on these boxes are Nvidia cards.The vga PCI card should installed in
a 32bit slot not the 64bit (long slots)slots. You have (3) -32bit slots
and (2) -64bit slots.If a video card is not supported in woody's stock
XFree86-4.1.x upgrade to 4.2.1 most cards are supported here.
PCI-USB cards are supported with a custom kernel(USB enabled). 
I hope this helps.
