Hello Tom,

I believe what you are looking for is DRM (Direct Rendering Manager) to e=
nable=20
DRI.  In the 2.4.18-26.9 kernel that is being tested for RH-7.2 for Alpha=
, we=20
do have the PCI radeon 7000 working on the Alpha Architecture with a litt=
le=20
mucking about.  So there is some hope that your 7500 might work.

We are using the default DRM from XFree86 4.3.0. In most cases, this work=
s=20
with the 4.1.0 XFree86 provided in RH-7.2. There are some problematic cas=
es=20
(such as the Radeon 7000) where the old DRM is still needed with this X
server. The "old" DRM modules are still provided in 2.4.18-26.9 with a -4=
=2E1.0=20
appended to their name. These can be selected with aliases in
/etc/modules.conf. For example, if you have a Radeon 7000 and have
trouble with 3D apps with the default DRM, you can select the old DRM by
adding this line to /etc/modules.conf:

       alias radeon radeon-4.1.0

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


